{"id":"44de8988-6733-478b-8d45-65de744c944d","object":"chat.completion","created":1785026992,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    passing = case.get('passing', [])\\n    failing = case.get('failing', [])\\n    required = case.get('required_difference', [])\\n    # compute ordered difference\\n    diff = [x for x in failing if x not in passing]\\n    if not diff:\\n        return {'isolated_difference': [], 'tests': 0}\\n    # oracle: passes iff not all required elements present\\n    def test(changes):\\n        return not set(required).issubset(set(changes))\\n    # ddmin algorithm (Zeller's delta debugging)\\n    D = diff[:]\\n    n = 2\\n    tests = 0\\n    # test full set\\n    tests += 1\\n    if test(D):\\n        # full set should fail, but if it passes, no reduction possible\\n        return {'isolated_difference': D, 'tests': tests}\\n    while n <= len(D):\\n        # compute chunk size\\n        chunk_size = (len(D) + n - 1) // n\\n        chunks = [D[i:i+chunk_size] for i in range(0, len(D), chunk_size)]\\n        reduced = False\\n        for i, chunk in enumerate(chunks):\\n            tests += 1\\n            if test(chunk):\\n                # chunk passes, test its complement\\n                complement = D[:i*chunk_size] + D[(i+1)*chunk_size:]\\n                tests += 1\\n                if test(complement):\\n                    # both pass; try next\\n                    continue\\n                else:\\n                    # complement fails -> reduce to complement\\n                    D = complement\\n                    reduced = True\\n                    break\\n            else:\\n                # chunk fails -> reduce to chunk\\n                D = chunk\\n                reduced = True\\n                break\\n        if reduced:\\n            n = 2\\n        else:\\n            n *= 2\\n    return {'isolated_difference': D, 'tests': tests}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task SE-DD-02. The output must be a JSON object with \"isolated_difference\" (array of strings) and \"tests\" (integer). Based on the description, we need to perform delta debugging (ddmin) on the difference between failing and passing test configurations. The payload contains \"passing\", \"failing\", \"required_difference\", \"unresolved_difference\". We must isolate a minimal causal difference between passing and failing configurations under the delta-debugging invariant. The \"required_difference\" is a list of elements that must be in the result? Actually, from typical delta debugging: we have a set of changes that cause failure. We have passing configuration (a set of changes) and failing configuration (another set). The difference is the changes that are present in failing but absent in passing. Then we run ddmin on that difference to find a minimal subset that still causes failure. But here we have \"required_difference\" which might be elements that are required to be in the isolated difference? And \"unresolved_difference\" may be elements that are not yet resolved? The function must return the isolated difference and number of tests performed.\n\nFrom the fixture examples: passing is [\"c0\",\"c1\",\"c2\"], failing is same plus [\"x0\",...,\"x5\"], so difference = [\"x0\",\"x1\",\"x2\",\"x3\",\"x4\",\"x5\"]. required_difference is [\"x4\",\"x5\"] in first case, [\"x2\",\"x4\"] second, [\"x2\",\"x5\"] third. So required_difference are the elements that must be included in the isolated difference? Possibly the objective is to find a minimal set that includes the required difference and still causes failure? Or the required difference is known to be part of the minimal cause? In delta debugging, we often have a failing case and a passing case; ddmin finds a minimal subset of the difference that still fails. But here we have \"required_difference\" which might be a set of elements that are 